As an initiate of the Goddess, I may not accept money from a man.	身為女神的入門弟子，我不得收受男子的錢財。
But, sir, of what use is grain to me?	但，大人，穀物對我有何用處？
How do you intend to feed them?	你打算如何餵養牠們？
Ione will take care of them now.	艾歐妮這下會照顧牠們了。
But what would that accomplish? Perhaps if you explained more clearly.	但那樣做能有何用處？或許你該解釋得更清楚些。
But I have no money.	但我身無分文。
And how do you propose to do that, Arthur?	那你打算如何做到，亞瑟？
She does not need any help.	她不需要任何協助。
Perhaps once her problem is solved, the poor girl will feel more like having a casual conversation.	或許等她的難題解決後，這可憐的女孩會更願意閒話幾句。
She is too distraught to speak.	她傷心欲絕，無法言語。
Only the Seeress can answer this question.	唯有女預言家能回答這個問題。
Seek your answers from the Seeress.	去向女預言家尋求答案吧。
That would not help.	那樣做無濟於事。
You thought me only a simple girl, but I am an initiate of the Goddess sent to watch and test you.	你以為我不過是個尋常女孩，但我其實是女神的入門弟子，奉命前來窺看並試煉你。
King Arthur, you have finished your tasks with this act of cleverness. Return to the Seeress for her judgment.	亞瑟王，你以此番機智完成了考驗。回去見女預言家，聽候她的裁定吧。
I dropped the cage and all my mistress' doves escaped. They will not come back and they are prize doves, hand fed by my mistress from hatchlings!	我把鳥籠摔了，我家主人的鴿子全飛走了。牠們不會回來的，而那些可是主人從雛鳥起親手餵養的名貴鴿子啊！
She trusted me with them. I dare not go back without them! Oh, misery!	她把牠們託付給我，我不敢空手回去見她！唉，我好命苦！
Mmmmm, so who are you, with lungs like the hamsin, the all-powerful wind? I see you are a foreigner, but from the look of you, not a very rich one. I only have time for rich men.	唔……你算什麼人物，說起話來竟像哈馬辛風那般氣勢逼人？看你是個外邦人，但瞧你這模樣，也不是什麼有錢人。我只有空應付有錢人。
Oh, it is you again. The mirror is wonderful. Well, what do you want? Speak up, I have a customer arriving soon.	喔，又是你。這面鏡子真是美極了。好吧，你想要什麼？快說，我馬上就有客人要到了。
You grow annoying. What do you want, infidel?	你越來越惹人厭了。你想要什麼，異教徒？
I do not think the word "girl" is appropriate for this strumpet.	『女孩』這個詞，用在這個蕩婦身上恐怕不太合適。
From the layers of paint upon her face, the excessive jewelry, the dyed hair and other signs, I would call this woman more than a trifle vain.	從她臉上厚厚的脂粉、滿身的首飾、染過的頭髮等種種跡象看來，我會說這女人虛榮得可不只一點點。
The woman, Mari, is not shy about displaying her attributes.	這女人，瑪麗，展露自己身段可是一點也不害臊。
The smell of her cheap ointments overwhelms even the odors of the gutter.	她那廉價脂粉的氣味，濃得連溝渠的臭味都蓋過去了。
She pays no attention to you at the moment.	她此刻並未理會你。
Chalas! Enough! I can hear you.	夠了！夠了！我聽得見你說話。
Ooh, big tough man. I am soooooo frightened. Better put away your sword, stupid infidel. One scream from me and the city guards will come running.	喔，好一個彪悍的男子漢，我可害怕得要死呢。你最好把劍收起來，蠢異教徒。我只消尖叫一聲，城裡的衛兵就會蜂擁而至。
I cannot stand here talking all day. I have business to do. If you want something, speak up.	我不能站在這裡跟你聊一整天，我還有生意要做。你若想要什麼，快說。
I am very unhappy right now. I know I am very beautiful, but I have no way to see my own beauty as others see it.	我此刻很不開心。我知道自己美豔動人，卻無從像旁人那樣，親眼見到自己的美貌。
And curse that wretched Ibrahim. He left me for his wife, of all things! At least I have kept his precious veil for revenge.	還有，去他的易布拉興，那個可惡的傢伙！他竟然為了自己的妻子甩了我！至少我留著他那條寶貝面紗，好好報復他。
My arms are not that long, foolish man, but... mmmm...I would dearly love to have that mirror.	我的手可沒那麼長，笨男人，不過……嗯……我倒是很想要那面鏡子。
If it were only money I wanted, I could have taken money from Ibrahim. But he dared to say I was vain because I wish to see my own beauty and he would have no part of it.	若我要的只是錢，大可直接向易布拉興要。但他竟敢說我虛榮，只因我想親眼見到自己的美貌，還說他不願插手這種事。
He probably gave you money, hoping to trick me. But it will not work. I will get what I want, or you get nothing.	他大概給了你錢，指望能騙過我。但這招行不通。我要拿到我想要的，否則你什麼也別想得到。
What would I want with a mule, silly man?	我要一頭騾子做什麼，傻男人？
I do not want that. Quit wasting my time.	我不要那個。別再浪費我的時間了。
Since you gave me the mirror, I will give you the veil as a favor. Wait a moment.	既然你給了我鏡子，我就賣你個人情，把面紗給你。等一下。
Well.....since you gave me the mirror, I will do you this favor. Wait a moment.	好吧……既然你給了我鏡子，我就賞你這個面子。等一下。
If you are a friend of Ibrahim, you are no friend of mine. He prefers his wife to me, the scoundrel. Let him suffer. He will never get the veil from me.	你若是易布拉興的朋友，那就不是我的朋友。那個無賴，寧可要他妻子也不要我。就讓他受苦去吧，這面紗他休想從我這裡拿走。
Unless, of course, you care to bring me something of greater value. Something that would allow me to see my great beauty as others see it.	當然，除非你願意帶些更有價值的東西來給我。能讓我像旁人一樣，親眼看見自己絕世美貌的東西。
I told you, I will exchange it for a way to see for myself how beautiful I am.	我說過了，我只肯用它換一樣能讓我親眼看見自己有多美的東西。
Whatever for? Your sword and armour are unequaled in quality.	何必呢？你的劍與盔甲，品質可是無與倫比。
You are more a boy than a man if you think that is what I sell.	你若以為我賣的是那種東西，那你不過是個乳臭未乾的男孩，稱不上男人。
I shudder to think what you would catch if you were to do so.	光是想到你那麼做會染上什麼病，我就不寒而慄。
Open my door to you? You could not afford me.	為你開門？你可付不起我的價碼。
I do not want to talk about the scoundrel. I hope he suffers because he will never get the veil from me.	我不想談那個無賴。我但願他不好過，因為這面紗他休想從我這裡拿走。
Mmmmm, I would dearly love him as a customer, but he has no time for me.	嗯……我倒很樂意讓他當我的客人，可惜他沒空理我。
He is a fat, prudish pig who will not do business with me.	他是個又胖又假正經的豬，不肯跟我做生意。
I only have time for rich men.	我只有空應付有錢人。
I will only be happy when I can see for myself how beautiful I am.	唯有能親眼看見自己有多美，我才會開心。
A woman as beautiful as me should have a mirror.	像我這樣美麗的女人，該有一面鏡子才是。
Her? Hah! Men think she is so beautiful, but she is nothing compared to me!	她？哼！男人們都以為她有多美，跟我一比，她算什麼！
Oh, quit wasting my time.	喔，別再浪費我的時間了。
My, Ibrahim must grow desperate indeed to send you after his precious veil. You may tell him it is not for sale.	哎呀，易布拉興想必是急壞了，才會派你來討他那條寶貝面紗。你可以告訴他，這東西不賣。
This overpainted trollop can do without that.	這濃妝豔抹的浪貨，沒有那個東西也活得下去。
You truly are a pest. Go away.	你真是煩人得很。走開。
This damsel is not in distress, Arthur.	這位小姐可不是什麼待救的佳人，亞瑟。
So, you are smarter than you look.	看來你比外表聰明些。
When I have the mirror, you may have the veil.	等我拿到鏡子，你就能拿到面紗。
It is true! I am as beautiful as they say! Even more so!	果然如此！我真如傳聞般美麗！甚至猶有過之！
Hmmph. And they say mirrors cannot lie. Hah!	哼，都說鏡子不會說謊。哈！
A most formidable looking man, but with an honest face. I would say he was previously a soldier who has gone into business selling what he knows best.	這人模樣威猛懾人，卻有一張誠實的臉。我猜他過去是個軍人，如今改行做起自己最擅長的買賣。
He wears an extremely good scimitar and dagger and from the looks of him, he knows how to use them.	他佩著一把上好的彎刀與一把匕首，看模樣，這兩樣兵器他都使得順手。
Mohammed is busy closing his shop.	穆罕默德正忙著打烊。
Perhaps you should move closer	或許你該再靠近一些
There is no-one inside my shop. I have closed up.	我店裡沒人了，我已經打烊了。
I would not annoy Mohammed by trying that when his shop is clearly closed.	店都明明已經打烊了，我可不會做這種事去惹惱穆罕默德。
Thought I would wait and see how you fared, warrior. I take it things do not go well. I am sorry to see it. If I were not about to leave on a long journey, I would take you in as my guest.	我想著在此等等，看你這一路走得如何，戰士。看來事情並不順利，我深感遺憾。若不是即將啟程遠行，我定會請你作客。
It does not seem to me that you have much use for your mule now. And a fine mule she is, too. Just the kind of mule I could use on a long journey.	依我看，你現在對這頭騾子似乎沒什麼用處了。而且是頭好騾子，正是我遠行路上用得著的那種。
I am sure you value your mule too highly to part with her. I certainly would.	我料想你太看重這頭騾子，捨不得割愛。換作是我，也是如此。
Your mule is safe, habib. I thought I had best remain and guard her against other thieves. They are a plague in Jerusalem.	你的騾子很安全，朋友。我想著最好留下來守著她，以防其他竊賊——耶路撒冷這種人可多得很。
I am not surprized you returned for her. She is an exceptionally well bred and well mannered mule. I use many mules in my travels and am a good judge.	你回來找她，我一點也不意外。她血統優良、性情又好，我行旅多用騾子，看得出好壞。
That truly is a very good mule. You undoubtedly value her very highly. If that were my mule, I would never sell her.	那真是頭上好的騾子。你想必十分珍視她。若換作是我的騾子，我絕不會出售。
You are wise not to waste your time chasing after him, habib. The thieves of Jerusalem are as slippery as eels.	你聰明，沒有浪費時間去追他，朋友。耶路撒冷的竊賊個個滑溜得像鰻魚。
A shame I must leave soon to join a caravan to Cairo, or you could be my guest. That is a very fine mule you have there, I notice. You must prize her highly.	真可惜我很快就得動身，加入前往開羅的商隊，不然你大可作我的客人。我注意到你那頭騾子相當出色，想必你十分珍視她。
I will ask Allah to aid you.	我會祈求阿拉助你一臂之力。
I fear you waited too long, Arthur. He is gone.	恐怕你等得太久了，亞瑟。他已經走了。
You would give me this excellent mule?! Habibi, you are either a holy man or a mad man. Still, you have my undying gratitude.	你願意把這頭上好的騾子送給我？！我的朋友啊，你不是聖人便是瘋子。但無論如何，我對你感激不盡。
You would not last long in Jerusalem without a sword. I could not consider buying your only weapon, magnificent though it is.	在耶路撒冷沒有劍，你撐不了多久。你僅有的這件武器，儘管精良，我實在不能買下它。
 I have many shields to sell and yours, though well made, has been through much travel and battle. Besides, you may well need it.	 我這裡有許多盾牌可賣，你這面盾牌雖做工精良，卻已歷經長途跋涉與征戰。再者，你恐怕還用得上它。
It is good armor, made after the fashion of the Romans, I see. But I am in the business of selling, not buying.	這副盔甲不錯，看樣式是仿羅馬人打的。不過，我做的是賣的生意，不做買的。
You look well equipped, habib, and I have closed up shop to go on a journey.	你裝備齊全，朋友，而我已經關店，準備啟程遠行了。
I sell only weapons and armor.	我只賣兵器與盔甲。
The mule looks very happy with Mohammed.	那頭騾子跟著穆罕默德，看來挺開心的。
She is yours, warrior. I am simply guarding her for you.	她是你的，戰士。我不過是替你看守著她罷了。
I do not know of such things. I am only a simple soldier turned merchant.	這種事我一概不知，我不過是個棄武從商的普通軍人。
There was another like you, but that was a some time ago. I do not know what became of him.	曾經有個跟你類似的人，不過那是好一陣子前的事了。我不知道他後來怎麼了。
She is a fine mule. I can see she has good bloodlines.	她是頭好騾子，一看便知血統優良。
That mongrel? He waits outside the gate and tries to trick people into paying him to enter! He is not very good at his fraud and most people are too smart to pay him.	那個混混？他守在城門外，想騙人付錢才讓人進城！他這騙術並不高明，大多數人都精明得不會上當。
I sell weapons of all kinds - swords, daggers, bows, maces, axes, spears and many other weapons. But I regret I have locked up as I must depart very soon to join a caravan.	我什麼兵器都賣——劍、匕首、弓、狼牙棒、斧頭、長矛，還有許多其他兵器。但可惜我已經上鎖打烊了，因為我很快就得動身加入商隊。
I deal with weapons only.	我只做兵器生意。
I travel with a caravan to Cairo.	我隨商隊前往開羅。
It is in Egypt.	它在埃及。
The wench lives above me, but I would avoid her company, if I were you.	那丫頭住在我樓上，但若我是你，我會少跟她來往。
I am sorry for your loss. That thief has done much mischief in the bazaar.	你的損失，我深感遺憾。那竊賊在市集裡沒少幹壞事。
It is a city of great interest, if one is careful enough.	只要夠謹慎，這是座頗值得一探的城市。
Eh? You jest. You know that means weapons.	咦？你在說笑吧。你明知道那指的是兵器。
I am not the wisest of men, habib, so I say as little as possible to hide my ignorance.	我算不上什麼聰明人，朋友，所以我盡量少開口，好掩飾自己的無知。
Not wise, habib. There are mercenary guards all over this city, eager to cut into pieces any foreigner foolish enough to cause trouble. I know. I have done it.	這可不明智，朋友。城裡到處都是雇傭衛兵，巴不得把任何蠢到惹事的外邦人剁成碎片。我很清楚，因為我幹過這種事。
Habibi, if you would truly part with this excellent mule, I will gladly give you all the money I have upon me. It is a goodly sum, but this fine mule is worth every coin.	我的朋友，你若真捨得割愛這頭上好的騾子，我樂意把身上所有的錢都給你。這是一筆不小的數目，但這頭好騾子值得每一枚錢幣。
In this purse you will find two dinars, that which is our gold coin. There are also dirhams, and these are silver, and some fals. A fals is a copper coin.	這錢囊裡有兩枚第納爾，也就是我們的金幣。此外還有些迪爾罕，那是銀幣，另外還有幾枚法爾斯。法爾斯是銅幣。
Since I see you do not understand, here is the way of it--4 fals are worth 1 dirham. 4 dirham are worth 1 dinar.	既然你不明白，我就把換算講給你聽——四法爾斯值一迪爾罕，四迪爾罕值一第納爾。
And now I must go and meet the caravan that awaits me. May Allah grant you good fortune.	現在我得去與等候我的商隊會合了。願阿拉賜你好運。
I must hurry now to meet my caravan. May Allah guide you.	我現在得快去與商隊會合。願阿拉指引你。
You wish to waste time with your lodestone when a thief has just stolen your purse?!	竊賊才剛偷走你的錢囊，你竟還想浪費時間擺弄指北針？！
So this is the bazaar of Jerusalem. Tiny shops line both sides of the street. And such smells! Delicious foods combined with the raw sewage in the gutter. Watch where you step.	這便是耶路撒冷的市集了。街道兩旁擠滿了小小的店鋪。那氣味真是——美味的食物混雜著溝渠裡的污穢，走路可得看清腳下。
Arthur! That little thief has grabbed your purse!	亞瑟！那個小賊搶走了你的錢囊！
There he goes, into an alley!	他往那條巷子跑了！
He does not look like he is stopping for anything.	看樣子他不會為任何事停下腳步。
You...you have brought this for me simply because I wanted it? No-one has ever shown me a kindness like this before.	你……你帶這個來給我，只因為我想要它？從沒有人曾這樣善待過我。
Your good example makes me ashamed! To think that I should be as callous as those I criticize and let this poor boy go hungry when I have food to spare.	你這番身教，讓我羞愧難當！我竟和自己譴責的那種人一樣冷漠，明明還有餘糧，卻放任這可憐的男孩挨餓。
Come here, little one. I will feed you and clothe you and raise you as my son in honor of this good man.	過來，孩子。我會給你飯吃、給你衣穿，並收養你為我的兒子，以此紀念這位善心人。
I shall name him Joshua.	我要為他取名約書亞。
Buy it? Does no-one do anything in this world without seeking gain? Very well, I will give you 3 fals for it, since you have gone to the trouble.	買下它？這世上難道人人做事都得圖點好處嗎？也罷，既然你費了這番工夫，我就給你三枚法爾斯。
Ya'Allah! It is the veil, the very veil! Habibi, you are forever my brother!	呀，阿拉啊！是這面紗，正是這面紗！我的兄弟，你永遠是我的兄弟！
I have had time to dwell upon my foolishness. I will never be unfaithful to my beloved wife again. Thank you! May you live long and bear many sons!	我已有時間好好反省自己的愚蠢。我再也不會對心愛的妻子不忠了。謝謝你！願你長命百歲，兒孫滿堂！
So, you are a scoundrel and a friend of Mari, no doubt. Expect no gratitude from me. Here is 1 dirham and be gone, or I will call the city guard to deal with you.	看來你是個無賴，想必還是瑪麗的朋友。休想從我這裡得到感激。這裡有一枚迪爾罕，快滾，否則我就叫城衛來對付你。
What shall I do? What shall I do? I have been betrayed by Mari the wicked, Mari the vain. For my brief moment of weakness, I shall lose my beloved wife.	我該如何是好？我該如何是好？我被瑪麗那惡毒又虛榮的女人給出賣了。只因我一時軟弱，就要失去我心愛的妻子。
You are a man. You will understand. I dallied but once with the woman, Mari, who lives above the shop of Mohammed. But I left behind a silken veil.	你是個男人，你會懂的。我只不過與那個住在穆罕默德店樓上的女人瑪麗鬼混過一次，卻把一條絲質面紗給留在了那裡。
Not any veil. A veil supreme in the mastery of the weaver's art, of glorious color and pattern. Mari refuses to return it to me.	那可不是普通的面紗，而是織藝登峰造極之作，色彩與紋樣皆美輪美奐。瑪麗死活不肯還給我。
I promised this veil to my wife as proof of my devotion. If I fail to bring it to her, she will leave me. I would do anything, pay anything, to avert that.	我曾答應把這面紗獻給妻子，作為我忠貞的憑證。若我拿不回它交給她，她便會離我而去。為了避免這件事，我什麼都願意做，什麼代價都願意付。
Poor thing probably cannot speak properly. Well, give him time. Sometimes silence is the greater virtue, eh?	這可憐人大概說不好話。罷了，給他點時間吧。有時候，沉默才是更大的美德，不是嗎？
No good trying to talk him. He never says a word. Not a tooth left in his head, anyway. He has been there for days, begging for crumbs.	跟他說話沒有用，他從不開口。反正他滿口牙也掉光了。他已經在那待了好幾天，乞討些殘羹剩飯。
Ah, it is a cruel world when no-one will help one another.	唉，這世道真是殘酷，竟沒有人願意互相幫助。
He is afraid to take money. It must remind him of some evil happening from his past.	他不敢收錢，想必是勾起了他過去某段不堪的往事。
He cannot eat it for he has lost most of his teeth, doubtless from starvation and hardship.	他吃不了這個，因為他的牙齒幾乎都掉光了，想必是飢餓與苦難所致。
Do not worry about him. He will have all the felafels his heart desires.	別擔心他了，他想吃多少法拉費都有。
Do not torment the boy, Arthur. You can see he is starving.	別折磨這男孩了，亞瑟。你也看得出他正忍飢挨餓。
He cannot eat the it for he has lost most of his teeth, doubtless from starvation and hardship.	他吃不了這個，因為他的牙齒幾乎都掉光了，想必是飢餓與苦難所致。
You have nothing to feed him, Arthur, though it is a worthy thought.	你身上沒有東西可以餵他，亞瑟，不過這份心意值得嘉許。
He is too afraid to take it.	他害怕得不敢收下。
